<article class="env-lemma" id="05F8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05F8">Lemma <span data-tag="05F8">37.30.2</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ be a morphism of finite type. Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  n_{X/Y} : Y \to \{ 0, 1, 2, 3, \ldots , \infty \}   \]
</div>
  <p> be the function which associates to $y \in Y$ the dimension of $X_ y$. If $g : Y' \to Y$ is a morphism then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  n_{X'/Y'} = n_{X/Y} \circ g  \]
</div>
  <p> where $X' \to Y'$ is the base change of $f$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This follows from Morphisms, Lemma <a href="/tag/02FY" data-tag="02FY">29.29.3</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>